## Construction discipline

```text
UNDERSTAND GOVERNANCE
→ IDENTIFY CURRENT AUTHORIZED OBJECTIVE
→ IMPLEMENT MINIMUM NECESSARY CHANGE
→ TEST → VALIDATE → COMMIT → STOP
```

**Forbidden default loop:** audit → redesign → audit → expand → refactor → audit.

Re-audit only when a real contradiction or blocker makes implementation unsafe.

## Do not

- Reduce MXT to a trading journal
- Optimize only for avoiding trades / equate risk avoidance with success
- Invent metrics or root cause from isolated outcomes
- Silently mutate Playbook/rules; contaminate history with hindsight
- Duplicate Stock File / Scout / Trade; invent architecture for modelable concepts
- Deploy production without an explicit release checkpoint

## Human vs system

**Owner:** intent, material decisions, adaptation authorization, rule changes, production release.  
**Agent:** evidence reconstruction, comparison, measurement, patterns, hypotheses, supported counterfactuals, experiment evaluation — do not dump routine analytical work back on the human.

## Older docs

Narrower superseded framings (strategic planning system, expectation database, gatekeeper/stop-you, capital-preservation-as-absolute-objective) may remain in the Library. **Do not delete or silently rewrite them.** Sealed Mission + Core Doctrine take precedence for identity and success criteria.

## After governance is recovered

Do not reopen sealed Mission/Doctrine or run documentation cleanup passes.

**Authorized learning path:** accumulate valid forward Cases (Scout → T0 → reality) → Edge Decomposition → human/AI analysis → hypotheses only with evidence → controlled change only when authorized.

Do not invent historical Cases or fabricate T0.
